# Tool log tables

Editable month/day record tables (daily bonus, island yields, …) share one pattern — do not invent a parallel one.

## Markup

```html
<table class="table table-striped log-table calc-table …">
  <tbody>
    <tr data-id="…" class="is-editing?">…</tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```

- Always include `.log-table` for pointer cursor + selected (`is-editing`) chrome
- Selected row: `class="is-editing"` while the left form is in update mode
- Page-specific extras (e.g. `.bonus-log-table`, `.farming-table`) are additive, not replacements

## JS

Use `bindLogTableRows` from `js/log-table.js` — do not re-bind `tbody tr[data-id]` click handlers ad hoc.

```js
import { bindLogTableRows } from './log-table.js';

bindLogTableRows(container, (id) => {
  // load row → fillForm → refresh log (re-apply is-editing)
});
```

## CSS

Base styles live on `.log-table` in `scss/main.scss`. Bonus-only states (gap, filter dim) stay under `.bonus-log-table`.
